export function renderHelp() {
  return `
playwright-screenshot — Responsive visual proof for dev-server UIs

USAGE
  playwright-screenshot <url> [output-path] [options]

DESCRIPTION
  Captures parallel screenshots of <url> at five canonical device viewports
  (mobile / mobile_safari / tablet_p / tablet_l / desktop), waits for the page to settle,
  writes PNGs (or JPGs) to disk, and prints a JSON summary on stdout.

  Use this for your own dev server, Storybook, or any URL you control.
  For authenticated third-party sites that require reusing a real logged-in
  Chrome session, use the live-session-capture skill instead.

  Engineering and QA agents MUST run this against any UI change before
  moving the ticket to in_review.

AUTO-SERVER BEHAVIOR (localhost URLs only)
  When the URL is a localhost URL with an explicit port (e.g. http://localhost:3101)
  the script manages the frontend dev server automatically:

  From a linked git WORKTREE:
    • Port free   → locate the frontend package (frontend/, ui/, app/, web/, or
                    root package.json), start its dev server, wait for it to respond,
                    capture, and leave it running for up to 5 minutes of inactivity.
    • Port in use by the same worktree   → attach and capture.
    • Port in use by a different worktree → error; use --attach-existing or a new port.
    • Port in use, no metadata            → error; use --attach-existing or a new port.

  From the MAIN checkout (non-worktree):
    • Port in use → capture immediately (server was started externally).
    • Port free   → error; start the server manually first.

  The temp server auto-stops after 5 minutes of inactivity (configurable via
  the UI_VISUAL_CAPTURE_IDLE_MS env var for testing).

ARGUMENTS
  <url>           Required. Full URL including scheme.
  [output-path]   Optional. One of:
                    - omitted: defaults via agent-fs when $AGENT_FS_BIN is set (preferred) —
                        · issue-scoped (cwd under <project>-worktrees/<key>/):
                            <agent-fs scratch>/ui-visual-capture-<issue-key>-<YYYY-MM-DD>/
                        · anonymous (main checkout / no issue):
                            <agent-fs scratch>/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<a|b|c…>/
                        Falls back to /tmp/ui-visual-capture/<...> ONLY when agent-fs
                        is unavailable. (The agent-fs PreToolUse guard blocks raw /tmp
                        writes, so the agent-fs default is what keeps captures sanctioned.)
                    - directory (existing or trailing /):  parent dir, named <viewport>.<ext> inside
                    - path with {viewport}:   substituted per viewport
                    - bare file path:         allowed only when capturing 1 viewport

  Issue keys are detected from the current working directory path segments
  (e.g. a worktree at .../gro-829/ → issue key "gro-829"; casing is preserved).
  Captures remain in session scratch. Local-only trackers require no upload or attachment;
  publication for an attachment-capable workflow is a separate explicit step.

OPTIONS

  Theme & resolution
    --theme=light|dark|system   Color scheme (default: system)
    --resolution=low|medium|high|native
                                low/medium = JPEG (token-light); high/native = PNG @2x (default: native)

  Capture mode
    --viewport-only             Capture visible region only (default: full page)
    --scroll-y=N                Scroll Y px before capture (mutually exclusive with --scroll-to)
    --scroll-to=SELECTOR        Scroll element into view before capture
    --clip-to=SELECTOR          Crop the capture to a single component: shoot only the
                                matched element's bounding box. Overrides full-page /
                                --viewport-only. Runs after --script, so you can open a
                                component into the state you want, then clip to it.

  Interaction
    --script PATH               Run an interaction script after navigation. The default export
                                is called with { page, viewport, context }. Enables video by default.
    --no-video                  Disable WebM recording when --script is set
    --video-fps=N               Frame extraction FPS for WebM contact sheets (default: 2).
                                Use 60 for frame-by-frame animation review.
    --contact-sheet-columns=N   Columns in generated WebM contact sheets (default: 4).
    --contact-sheet-thumb-width=N
                                Thumbnail width in generated WebM contact sheets (0 = source width).

  Auth
    --auth-token TOKEN          Sets Authorization: Bearer TOKEN on all requests
    --storage-state PATH        Playwright storageState JSON (cookies + localStorage).
                                The URL's origin must match the captured origin.
    --header KEY=VALUE          Extra HTTP header (repeatable; split on first =)

  Stability
    --wait-until=load|domcontentloaded|networkidle
                                Navigation readiness signal (default: networkidle).
                                Use domcontentloaded for Storybook dev-server iframes.
    --stable-timeout=MS         Max DOM-stable wait after navigation (default: 10000)

  Selection / output
    --viewports=LIST            Subset or per-name overrides, e.g. mobile,desktop, mobile=375,
                                desktop=1440, or mobile=80x48 for exact width+height.
                                Canonical names: mobile, mobile_safari, tablet_p, tablet_l, desktop.
                                mobile_safari is 390x664 (iPhone Safari with top+bottom browser chrome) and is
                                mandatory for any fixed/sticky overlay (modal, sheet, drawer, nav, toast).

  Server
    --attach-existing           Capture from the server already running on the requested port,
                                even if it was started from a different worktree.

  Misc
    --help, -h                  Show this help and exit

OUTPUT FORMAT
  stdout is a single JSON object:
    {
      "status": "ok" | "partial" | "error",
      "outputDir": "/abs/path",
      "server": {
        "mode": "started" | "attached" | "attached-explicit" | "external" | null,
        "port": 3101,
        "worktreeRoot": "/abs/path/to/worktree",
        "packageDir": "/abs/path/to/frontend",
        "pid": 12345,
        "logPath": "/tmp/ui-visual-capture/servers/3101.log"
      },
      "captures": [
        { "viewport": "mobile",   "status": "ok",    "path": "/abs/.../mobile.png",   "videoPath": "/abs/.../mobile.webm" },
        { "viewport": "tablet_p", "status": "error", "error": "..." },
        ...
      ]
    }

  \`server\` is null when the URL is not a localhost URL or is an implicit port.

EXIT CODES
  0  All viewports captured successfully
  1  At least one viewport failed
  2  Bad arguments
  3  Playwright module not found in any ancestor node_modules
  4  Server error: conflict, startup failure, or server not running when required

EXAMPLES
  Basic capture from a worktree (server auto-starts on port 3101):
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3101

  Same-day second run reattaches to the running server automatically:
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3101/dashboard

  Capture from a server started by a different worktree (explicit opt-in):
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3101 --attach-existing

  Capture from an already-running server on main checkout:
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3000/dashboard --theme=dark

  Footer in viewport-only mode:
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3000 --scroll-to='[data-testid="footer"]' --viewport-only

  Crop to a single component (precise element bounding box):
    playwright-screenshot 'http://localhost:6006/iframe.html?id=atoms-button--primary' \\
      --clip-to='[data-testid="button"]' --wait-until=domcontentloaded

  Scripted interaction with video, only mobile + desktop:
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3000/meals \\
      --script ./interactions/open-meal-edit.mjs \\
      --viewports=mobile,desktop

  Authenticated route via stored session:
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3000/account --storage-state ./.auth/state.json

  Custom output paths with placeholder:
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3000 '/tmp/run/{viewport}.png'

  Token-light captures for agents that read the file back into context:
    playwright-screenshot http://localhost:3000 --resolution=low

INTERACTION SCRIPT CONTRACT
  Default export is an async function called once per viewport:

    // interactions/open-meal-edit.mjs
    export default async function ({ page, viewport, context }) {
      await page.locator('[data-testid="meal-card"]').first().click();
      await page.locator('[data-testid="edit-meal"]').click();
      await page.waitForSelector('[data-testid="meal-edit-sheet"]');
      // The screenshot is taken AFTER this returns, against the resulting page state.
    }

  An exception aborts that one viewport (status: "error") but does not abort siblings.
  When --script is set, video recording is on by default; pass --no-video to disable.
`.trimStart();
}
